# Pipeline not being flushed on PMP register clears

- Source URL: https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex/pull/2214

In [this commit](https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex/commit/46404cf86f60f72fb84a2bc693d2ab08011bdb37) the pipeline was made to flush on changes to PMP registers, changes made via `CSR_OP_CLEAR` however are missed.

This is likely because prior to this commit only mstatus and mie were listed, and clearing is safe for those.

This meant that instructions being fetched were passing PMP checks which they should not have been.

## Fetched Issue/PR Details

Title: [rtl] Flush pipe on all CSR modifications (PR #2214)

Description: This fix addresses issue #2193, where bit clears in PMP-related CSRs weren't immediately applying to instructions already in the fetch stage due to missing pipeline flushes. The solution flushes the pipeline on all CSR modifications to make the system more resilient against similar oversights in the future.

Key Changes:
- CSR address reading optimization: Routes CSR addresses directly from the decoder to the ibex_cs_registers module rather than through operand muxes, improving timing.
- Pipeline flush on CSR modifications: Implements a whitelist where most CSR writes trigger pipeline flushes, but specific CSRs (mscratch, mepc) are excluded since they don't affect instruction execution in the fetch stage.

Notable Discussion:
- Performance considerations: Reviewers raised concerns about CSR write frequency during exception handling. The author acknowledged that while some CSR operations (like csrrw for stack switching) are performance-sensitive, the actual performance impact is limited since Ibex has only a single fetch stage and CSR instructions typically aren't in tight loops.
- Whitelist rationale: The team determined that mscratch and mepc don't require flushes - mscratch is purely a temporary storage location, and mepc is only read during exception returns, not during fetch-stage instruction execution.

